@coderabbitai Valid, but the gap predates this PR, so it is tracked as GH#40018 (t19312) rather than fixed here.

I verified it against current code. When `_hrff_check_release_claim` runs without a projection line, `dispatch-release-claim.jq:46-48` returns `released`, `headless-runtime-release-claim.sh:67-69` treats that as a skip, `_hrff_release_dispatch_claim_attempt` returns 0 at line 922, and `_release_dispatch_claim` clears the retry row at line 798. None of those lines change in this PR. The gap affects every caller of `_release_dispatch_claim`, not only the exit trap.

This PR makes the exit trap publish the release before the terminal lease. Its only failure case here (publication succeeds, then projection fails) leaves the issue held until the stale sweep. Before this PR, every exit-trap prelaunch failure ended in that state. GH#40018 extends the existing `blocked` persisted-release projection (`headless-runtime-failure.sh:940-947`) to every reason during replay, and keeps the retry row when projection fails.

